                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really wanted to like this game, but it has way too much of what I call 'developer difficulty' added to it. That means the developers created it and knows every single thing about the game, and how to best take advantage of all the little secrets. \r\n\r\nAny complaint simply gets a 'get this gadget' response. As if 'getting that gadget' is some easy task that is quickly found. Then you have to add it to your ship and hope the next encounter does not simply blow it up along with most of your ship. So you basically start over with each encounter unless you get lucky with left over scrap. But then, you have very limited time to collect that scrap, and add it to your ship before time runs out and you are sent to the next sector with a half built ship.\r\n\r\nThe biggest complaint many gamers have with the game is the timer for building your ship after a fight. The devs have done nothing to address that complaint except tell you to find the time+ components for your ship, like that is some easy solution. A better solution would be an option for the player to decide on less or more time, or to turn it off completely.\r\n\r\nI am not that good a player I guess since I could not get past the 2nd jump, always getting my ship completely demolished each time. I finally gave up and uninstalled the game once, then installed it years later and still could not progress much at all. Which is a shame because I like the games premise and would really like a more entertaining game without all the difficulty drama.",
